  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Internews: Media Literacy and Moldovan Media 2022-2025 - Internews: Media Literacy Advancement and Support to Moldovan Media</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Internews: Media Literacy and Moldovan Media 2022-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen kommer att bidra till att uppn&#xe5; resultat under m&#xe5;lomr&#xe5;de nr. 1: &quot;M&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter, demokrati, r&#xe4;ttsstatsprincipen och j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet: B&#xe4;ttre demokratisk samh&#xe4;llsstyrning och respekt f&#xf6;r m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter och r&#xe4;ttsstatsprincipen&quot;.
F&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla att alla m&#xe4;nniskor &#xe4;r fullt bemyndigade med de nyheter och information de beh&#xf6;ver fokuserar Internews p&#xe5; konsolidering av civilsamh&#xe4;llet och st&#xf6;djande av processer f&#xf6;r icke-statliga organisationers koalitioner, i syfte att fr&#xe4;mja demokratiska principer och v&#xe4;rderingar i Republiken Moldavien.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention will contribute to the achievement of outputs under result area nr. 1 &quot;Human rights, democracy, the rule of law and gender equality:  Better democratic governance and respect for human rights and the rule of law&quot;. 
To ensure that all people are fully empowered with the news and information they need, Internews concentrates on consolidation of civil society and supporting the processes of non-governmental organizations&apos; coalitions in order to promote democratic principles and values in the Republic of Moldova.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the Project is to contribute towards the growth of a diverse, independent and financially viable media landscape in Moldova and to empower Moldovan youth to navigate their complex information environment.

The design of the activities, and the implementation approach have been developed as a direct result of the periodic organisational capacity assessment conducted by Internews on all key partners. The activities are structured in the following groups planned to be implemented during 36 months: 

SO1: Consolidate financial sustainability, editorial development and management support to independent media outlets
Using the evidence-based approach, Internews will provide support to regional and national key partner media through sub-granting and tailored mentoring and consulting to 1) widen the reach of regional key partner media, their engagement with audiences and financial sustainability; 2) consolidate the support provided to national key partner media and bolster their capacity for financial independence. Internews previous project work has demonstrated that the most efficient way to support change within partner newsrooms is through intensive tailored mentoring.

SO2: Strengthen the media literacy and critical thinking of Moldovan youth, including vulnerable groups
Internews will issue a sub-grant to IJC to lead on the activities within SO2. The project will improve the media literacy tools by 1) revising the outdated Media Education textbooks and digitising them, 2) supporting teachers to integrate the new tools in teaching, 3) opening access to Media Education tools for children with special needs by providing them with accessible textbooks and video lessons.</narrative>
  </description>
